<v SPEAKER_3>That's one in three. By 2016 the number was only 2%. In the late 1970s, 60% of 12th graders in the US said they read a book or a magazine almost every day. By 2016 only 16% did. And this is despite the fact that we could, you know, you could be talking about digital content. It's just not happening. People are in the world of Tiktok, it used to be once upon a time they're in the world of Facebook or Twitter. And they are not engaging in long-form reading, even in the sense of reading articles in newspapers or magazines. So that's a really dramatic shift.

